{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"clumpish-appetitive-harrier","creation_channel":"cli","description":"`.github/complexity-baseline.json` is a shrink-only *gate* protecting a freely-growable *baseline*,\nand unlike `.github/module-size-limit.txt` it has **no CI lock at all**\n(`grep 'complexity-baseline' .github/workflows/` returns zero hits).\n\n## Two distinct defects\n\n**1. No lock.** The module-size limit is locked against `main` in\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:363-373`: CI fetches `main`, compares the limit value, and\nhard-errors on any change, so raising it requires an administrator override. The complexity baseline\nhas no equivalent — any contributor change to it lands like ordinary code.\n\n**2. The baseline can be GROWN silently.** `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` guards the\nschema, sortedness, `ceiling > 15`, `stale == []`, and `len(ceilings) == live`. Those prevent\n*raising* an existing ceiling and prevent stale entries. They do NOT prevent **adding a new entry**:\nwrite a new function at complexity 30, add its baseline entry, and `live` grows with it — count\nmatches, `stale` stays empty, gate green. There is no assertion that the entry count is monotonically\nnon-increasing and no maximum size.\n\nNet effect: the ratchet only ratchets on functions already in the file. New complexity enters freely.\n\n## Do NOT copy the module-size lock's fail-open\n\n`_build-and-test.yml:372-374` — if the `git fetch` of `main` fails, the lock emits\n`::warning::` and skips the comparison. The comment says \"the absolute cap below still applies\",\nwhich is true but misleading: the cap then runs at the **unverified** `$LIMIT` from the current\nbranch. A change raising `800` to `5000` passes on any run where that fetch flakes. The new lock must\nfail CLOSED when it cannot establish the base value, and the module-size lock should be fixed to\nmatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] CI locks `.github/complexity-baseline.json` against `main`: a change to the file fails the\n      build unless an administrator overrides the gate, matching the module-size limit's posture\n- [ ] The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched — no `::warning::`-and-continue\n- [ ] `_build-and-test.yml`'s module-size lock is changed to fail closed for the same reason\n- [ ] A test asserts the baseline entry count is monotonically non-increasing against `main`, so a\n      new high-complexity function cannot be admitted by adding a baseline entry\n- [ ] Adding a new function above the C901 threshold fails CI even when a matching baseline entry is\n      added in the same change\n- [ ] Legitimate baseline SHRINKAGE (a function refactored below its ceiling, entry removed) still\n      passes without an override\n- [ ] The intended posture — who may change the baseline and how — is documented next to the file","id":"47e9-728e-ba93-485e","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","priority":1,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Lock complexity-baseline.json in CI and make the baseline shrink-only"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786054147160893001,"uuid":"59a1a6a8-c7bc-4198-89bf-590f3c2bf2c8"}